export anchor CassetteDeckStyle:
    number: 332
    screen: MusicPlayer
    name: Cassette deck
    idea: The player is a front loading cassette deck, with a tape window of turning reels, a mechanical counter, two amber VU meters with needles, a row of chrome piano keys for transport and the queue typed on the cassette insert card.
    base: dark
    palette:
        deck: #151517, the page, the deck body and the style sheet
        ribbed: #1e1e21, body ribs, the insert card and the list row
        bezel: #3a3a3f, window, meter and counter bezels, and rules
        chrome: #c9ccd1, piano keys and toggle caps, as a gradient from #eceef0 to #a6aab0
        keyInk: #111214, legends printed on chrome
        legend: #e6e6ea, panel legends and text
        legendDim: #a8a8b2, units, small print and secondary lines
        meterAmber: #ffc56b, VU faces, the lyric memo, the playing lamp, the progress fill and focus
        peakRed: #ff8a6a, the VU red zone above zero, marked with plus figures
        tapeBrown: #3a2a1e, tape wound on the reels, decorative
    type:
        Three voices. Panel legends use Eurostile, Microgramma, Bank Gothic,
        Arial Narrow in caps, with the title at clamp 24 to 34px at 700 and
        0.12em tracking, and small legends at 11px at 700 with 0.2em. The
        counter and lyric memo use ui-monospace and Menlo, the counter 28px
        at 700. The insert card uses Courier New and Courier at 16px. Body
        text is Helvetica Neue at 14px.
    layout:
        A ribbed deck beside a side column. The deck header reads
        BRIGHTWORK SOUND and Stereo cassette deck, now playing. A tape
        window with an inset shadow shows a dark cassette with a beige
        label handwritten Low Tide, side A, and two white six spoke reels
        turning in brown tape. Beside it two amber backlit VU meters, VU L
        and VU R, with ticks from minus 20 to plus 3, a red zone and white
        needles just below zero. Under them a four wheel mechanical counter
        reads 0214 beside Tape counter and of 4 38, then an Output level
        fader with a chrome cap at 70 percent over a 0 to 10 scale. Below
        sit HARBOUR LIGHTS in wide caps with the artist and album, then a
        black Lyric memo display in amber monospace with the current line
        behind a chevron and the next line dimmer. A row of four touching
        chrome piano keys follows, PREV, PLAY pressed down with a lit
        amber lamp and the word PLAYING, PAUSE and NEXT, then three small
        chrome toggles, Shuffle Off, Repeat Off and Liked On with a heart.
        A thin amber progress bar with the elapsed and total time closes
        the deck. The side column holds the insert card, a spine headed
        Insert, up next and Side A over five typed rows with number, title,
        artist and time, then Tape shelf, your library as three cassette
        spines with a coloured edge and song counts, and chrome keys for
        Albums, Artists and Podcasts. Below 1100px the side column moves
        under the deck, and below 760px the deck stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px deck padding, 16 to 20px between modules and 2px seams between piano keys.
    density: Medium. A full machine face, with the queue on a separate card.
    corners: 6px deck and meter bezels, 12px tape window, 2px keys and fields, 4px insert card.
    borders: 1px bezel rings around the window, meters and counter wheels, a double rule under the insert spine and 2px ribs across the body.
    shadows: Raised chrome keys cast a hard 0 4px 0 black. The pressed key drops to 0 1px 0 and sits 3px lower. The window has an inset shadow.
    icons:
        Classic transport glyphs printed on each key above its word. The
        pressed Play key shows a lit lamp and the word PLAYING. Toggles say
        Off or On, with On in amber. The current lyric has a chevron.
    focus: A 2px amber outline offset 3px on every key, field and card row.
    tone: Hardware legends, such as Tape counter, Output level, Lyric memo, Insert and Tape shelf.
